From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 11] ttm: one DMA binding per tt on illumos

TTM's pool DMA-maps every allocation chunk with dma_map_page(). LinuxKPI
cannot give a page more than one page of physically contiguous memory
(alloc_pages() of a higher order fails), so every chunk is one page, and
on illumos every mapping is a DDI DMA handle of its own: 2600 bytes on
rootnex, two thirds of the 4 KiB page it maps.

- ttm_tt.h, ttm_tt.c: the tt's binding (struct ttm_tt illumos_dma),
  cleared when the tt is set up;
- ttm_pool.c: the pool maps no page by itself; once a tt is fully
  allocated, LinuxKPI's lkpi_dma_map_pages() binds all its pages with
  one handle (through a vmap() of them) and fills dma_address;
  ttm_pool_free() and ttm_pool_backup() unmap the tt before they free
  any page; ttm_pool_unmap() does nothing. The dma_alloc_coherent()
  pool (TTM_ALLOCATION_POOL_USE_DMA_ALLOC) is unchanged.

License: MIT files; applied to the pinned Linux tree.

